      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mry6aitps6t7d8ph",
          "message": {
            "text": "Reader precedence is `markdown ?? text`, not the other way round.\n\nSARIF carries a message in two forms. §3.11.9 requires `text` whenever `markdown` is present, but only so the message stays viewable in a consumer that cannot render formatting — it explicitly says such a consumer \"SHALL ignore the markdown property and use the text property instead\". Glassbox *can* render it (`renderNoteMarkdown`, §20.6), so the inverse applies: prefer `markdown`.\n\nBefore this, the reader took `message.text` only, so a third-party producer writing the spec-correct pair (plain prose in `text`, rich formatting in `markdown`) had its formatting silently discarded.\n\nThe helper exists so `coalesceFile`'s redundancy key uses the same precedence as display — keying on `text` alone would collapse two notes that render differently but share a plain-text fallback.",
            "markdown": "Reader precedence is `markdown ?? text`, not the other way round.\n\nSARIF carries a message in two forms. §3.11.9 requires `text` whenever `markdown` is present, but only so the message stays viewable in a consumer that cannot render formatting — it explicitly says such a consumer \"SHALL ignore the markdown property and use the text property instead\". Glassbox *can* render it (`renderNoteMarkdown`, §20.6), so the inverse applies: prefer `markdown`.\n\nBefore this, the reader took `message.text` only, so a third-party producer writing the spec-correct pair (plain prose in `text`, rich formatting in `markdown`) had its formatting silently discarded.\n\nThe helper exists so `coalesceFile`'s redundancy key uses the same precedence as display — keying on `text` alone would collapse two notes that render differently but share a plain-text fallback."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/review-notes/store.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 196,
                  "endLine": 206,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * The displayed body of a note. SARIF carries a message in two forms: `markdown`\n * (GitHub-Flavored, the formatted form) and `text` (the plain-text fallback that\n * must accompany it). Per SARIF 2.1.0 §3.11.9 only a consumer that *cannot*\n * render formatted text is required to fall back to `text` — Glassbox renders\n * markdown (`renderNoteMarkdown`), so it prefers `markdown` and a producer that\n * writes a spec-correct plain/rich pair keeps its formatting.\n */\nfunction noteBody(r: NoteResult): string {\n  return r.message?.markdown ?? r.message?.text ?? '';\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
